+## 2024-05-18 - Reuse Memoized Data in Drag Handlers
+**Learning:** Re-sorting arrays dynamically in drag-and-drop handlers (e.g., onDragEnd) introduces unnecessary processing overhead and can cause visual stuttering during high-frequency events.
+**Action:** Always reuse the already-memoized sorted lists (e.g., `sortedTargetRecruits`) when calculating index shifts for array moves, rather than recreating and re-sorting the original array from scratch.
